-- title:
--   The dlog injection Pic⁰[p]↪Ω_{F/K}, pinned by its recipe
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $F$ a field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure, and $p$ a prime with $\operatorname{char} K = p$. Let $t \in F$ be transcendental over $K$, assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(t)$ generated by $t$ and separable over it, and assume $D_{F/K}(t) \neq 0$ in the module $\Omega[F\!/\!K]$ of Kähler differentials. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; a divisor is a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on places, $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ is the group of divisors in the kernel of the degree homomorphism modulo those of the form $v \mapsto v.\mathrm{ord}\, f$ for some $f \neq 0$, and $\mathrm{Pic0.torsion}\ K\ F\ p$ is the subgroup of elements annihilated by $p$. The assertion is that there exists an additive homomorphism $\delta$ from this $p$-torsion subgroup to $\Omega[F\!/\!K]$ which is injective and satisfies: for every $x$ in the subgroup, every degree-zero divisor $E$ whose class is $x$, and every $g \neq 0$ in $F$ with $p \cdot E(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}\, g$ for all places $v$, one has $\delta(x) = g^{-1} \cdot D_{F/K}(g)$.
--
--   This is the logarithmic-differential embedding of the $p$-torsion of the Jacobian of a curve in characteristic $p$ into the space of differentials of its function field, in the pinned form that prescribes the value $dg/g$ on every representative pair $(E,g)$ with $pE = \operatorname{div} g$ — the form needed for compatibility with correspondences and automorphisms. It is used in the study of the $p$-torsion of modular Jacobians, in particular in the statements about Hecke operators on $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ modulo $\ell$ and about torsion of the curves $X_1$ that cite it.
